<img class="map-background" src="/map-wallpaper-muted.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />

<style>
  .map-background {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    /* Never narrower than the viewport, so its edges never show on wide
       screens. Below 1440 it keeps its designed scale and crops. */
    width: max(1440px, 100vw);
    min-height: 100vh;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top center;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-drag: none;
    /* The 30% saturation is baked into map-wallpaper-muted.svg (the CSS saturate() matrix applied to each colour), so
       only opacity is left here. A CSS filter on this fixed layer made Firefox redraw it on every scroll frame: 17 of
       61 frames ran slow at 1440 wide, 4 without it (2026-10-10). Opacity composites on the GPU for free. The source
       colours stay in map-wallpaper.svg. */
    opacity: 0.45;
  }
</style>
